ara, Coconut, Pyāla, Panasa and various other trees.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.682,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-26-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7026003","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2775a9522b93577d7f82435d869d85ef175c5d351ae07df1bff3dfe6373e84ce","compact":"bd5202d580e395debfefe8d173a9ec8df81a39a4b370cf0743cf54f5fee501fc","nasal":"c4da2935db2240b1e4eaa84e1c7b9213dbbf351799c3c003663ea89952524c66"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-26-4","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":26,"verse":4,"english":"There was audible in the house of the lord of riches, the sweet music of the assembled Apsarās like to the sound of the bell.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.83,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-26-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7026004","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6556890f7c10451dfadd4caf05f715cc3d77f52186ce93a500f572b6d3ef50c2","compact":"16514b083c680266849b40bb753edf2a57aba2505db99134158557f7fc6d6884","nasal":"2c32dd8194cc11d33dcb77a9c4ad8a3089863667e8f99fc63c3161a2219285da"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-26-5","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":26,"verse":5,"english":"Being shaken by the wind the nectar-smelling trees made the hill fragrant with the shower of flowers.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.86,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-26-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7026005","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3dabbe33ffc6f5b828cd118d93c8bf2a29fd842cd4004d46c568fc2e3ba4941e","compact":"6dd218bf3481c6558206aad826a098379ee27f1031864bcd1c09c8e16be4103c","nasal":"5d6a3cfd75382bc8f107f8bd11b096d21cf37854d4fcbd996ed15a7e1804f1f6"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-26-6","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":26,"verse":6,"english":"And carrying the 