as like the moon, eye brows like the excellent bows, thighs like the trunks of elephants and palms soft as leaves. She was seen by Rāvana as proceeding in the midst of soldiers.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.955,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-26-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7026011","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f96d6b062da3a4ce8d7899c2162eb55d6be6e2e277875d3d1bccf3f26407e01b","compact":"c09cff280fc7fee2c3df644fa03d04484636b853da69dd49414112a12430d359","nasal":"747252d07b1d15d5fca59468c42a01452b02bba8056a195f1acc31521838aa0d"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-26-12","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":26,"verse":12,"english":"Having got up and been influenced by lust he took her, shameful as she was, by the hand and smiling said.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.369,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-26-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7026012","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"faa5a84eece6d7caa3fde22e911884756811cca799524179dfc5381517e68a05","compact":"34ddb97be9966e63e029e51f8fa96ec64f001b9a7d682dd878c534de866fb938","nasal":"915d988a520847857bddaaca74c94d07315d8d4fbb9b1dcf76e7cba92f701ab7"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-26-13","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":26,"verse":13,"english":"Where are you going, O beautiful damsel? Whom are you going of your own accord to satisfy? Whose prosperous time has appeared, with whom you shall enjoy?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-26-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7026013","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"65c92d9aee615b6b64fa1889b8ecc0d0b0e1a2063e7a1573cdcedf09e5fcd618","compact":"268898057ec3beae5d77107e9d8377d01cdbc55b18c3f8d90c8472e747de6204","nasal":"268898057ec3beae5d77107e9d8377d01cdbc55b18c3f8d90c8472e747de6204"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-26-14","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":26,"verse":14,"english":"Who shall be satisfied with drinking the nectar of your mouth smelling like lotus?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.712,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-26-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7026014","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2587b36939d260bf570cb6aea40935455ba55a75a8beff203bba5cfba7ee17a4","compact":"2a2ac8385aa8c161bff851d0784d04fc32140d834ef3817d53bf320dfa199c2e","nasal":"d211ed5f15922b3041e77c7ed908b0cd9da2f8de8f305b06789d6ba2c1cac717"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-26-15","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":26,"verse":15,"english":"Whose breast, O fare damsel, your rising breast beautiful like two golden pots closely placed, shall touch?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.877,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-26-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7026015","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c8db03c06985e47a96e5c8621c20cf1208024da88a46d77fe43e9351bc44a76c","compact":"13eb713a1e5b79dc338b606910849fc90f4cd86b8452518aaa29fcb40f77150d","nasal":"6060b1def03dc4158cb4368acc01cd39b5d7ca438f1c78476ae8b31065d67fec"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-26-16","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":26,"verse":16,"english":"Who will go to bestride today your large thigh resembling a disc of gold, encircled by a golden chain and which was like the form of a heaven.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.742,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-26-19"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7026016","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8e3b21f41e1af2e20277b246fcc592211c8731d1b74959677447f4e7424a04f2","compact":"c3098c1bb5d70ab5487d8cafb5