been the wife of my son, you would have been my daughter-in-law.” Whereto Rambha replied. “Truly it is; I am, by virtue, the wife of your son, O foremost of Raksasas. Your brother Vaiśravana has a son, dearer than his life, celebrated in the three worlds under the name of Nalkūbara. In virtue he is like to a Brahmin, in prowess he equals a Kşatriya, in anger he is very fire and in patience he is like the earth. I have been thus directed by that Lokapāla's son. For him I have adorned my person with these ornaments. I am not attached to any body else but him. O king, O slayer of foes, by virtue of (this relation) is behove you to save me. And that virtuous-souled one is anxiously expecting me.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.431,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-26-26","DUTT-7-26-27"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7026026","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"41ad94b60a2b1c90ca1e4854f761d018e422474c35d8834f2dda2de995750b4d","compact":"ffa84e21e1ba237ff6d521de67eee1c8382ab53b9822278a0b737d5ad49a4fd5","nasal":"ffa84e21e1ba237ff6d521de67eee1c8382ab53b9822278a0b737d5ad49a4fd5"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-26-27","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":26,"verse":27,"english":"For him I have adorned my person with these ornaments. I am not attached to any body else but him. O king, O slayer of foes, by virtue of (this relation) is behove you to save me. And that virtuous-souled one is anxiously expecting me.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.954,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-26-27"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7026027","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"92dae5f6b4ca557ef0759eac6b2a6014a29a17fb85367e910bfeec1c16ff02f8","compact":"04f905b160ea1bf0ba615ec106c6f0c2675b910a92059ca9657625f7ec891214","nasal":"04f905b160ea1bf0ba615ec106c6f0c2675b910a92059ca9657